<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Redon Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">832</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Abbey of Saint-Sauveur de Redon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Redon Abbey, the Benedictine abbey of Saint-Sauveur at Redon in eastern Brittany, was founded in 832 by the monk Conwoion with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a>. It became the leading monastery of Carolingian Brittany, and its cartulary, recording hundreds of land grants, is a key source for Breton society and the rule of the machtierns in the 9th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/redon-abbey.jpg" alt="Redon Abbey" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Redon_-_Abbatiale_Saint-Sauveur_et_Mairie_-_Cylindrique_-_20090704.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
